findings.body:
The source keeps `url == trusted` as an alternative that needs no `PUSH_GATE_REMOTES` entry (L692-695). The README relies on this: "Without the variable, every push of a branch the plans do not list asks."

The diff moved every plans test onto `fixture.gate()`, which lists `{root}/ git@example.invalid:`. That list prefix-matches the plan URL `{root}/remote.git`. The affected tests are:
- `gate_with_plan`, plus `expect_planned` and the remap loop built on it.
- `reads_a_plans_line_without_its_newline`.
- `reads_plans_only_from_the_file_the_environment_names`.
- `reads_no_plans_from_a_relative_path`.

Before this PR they used a bare `hook("push-gate")`. The two tests that change `PUSH_GATE_REMOTES` set no plans file.

As a result, a mutant such as `trusted_match && probed_match` survives the suite. Under it, an approved plan would quietly stop being enough on its own.

Source: https://github.com/AlexisBalayre/claude-code-config/blob/c27788450dd927d8bef7e39efcd92828bba05ea7/tools/hooks-rs/src/push_gate.rs#L688-L697

Tests: https://github.com/AlexisBalayre/claude-code-config/blob/c27788450dd927d8bef7e39efcd92828bba05ea7/tools/hooks-rs/tests/push_gate.rs#L78-L90

Suggested test, next to `reads_a_plans_line_without_its_newline`:

```rust
#[test]
fn defers_for_a_planned_url_without_the_remotes_variable() {
    let fixture = Fixture::new("plans-unlisted");
    let plans = fixture.path("plans-bare");
    write(&plans, &format!("feature/new {}\n", fixture.at("remote.git")));
    let mut gate = hook("push-gate");
    gate.env("AGENT_APPROVED_PLANS", plans);
    expect_decision(&mut gate, "none", &fixture.at("w"), PUSH_NEW, "");
}
```
